From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:43:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: apple: Add T6040 with the second state off by
 default

The T6040 (M4 Pro) cores power down in a plain WFI: they come back with
x0-x15 and the FP/SIMD registers lost, which the arm64 idle code
already saves on this SoC. The CPU PD state requests a power-down by
setting bits in CYC_OVRD, and iBoot locks that register on the M4
SoCs, so the state cannot run here. T8140 has the same properties and
already runs both entries through WFI; do the same when the device tree
has an "apple,t6041-cpuidle" node.

The driver is new on this SoC, so mark the second entry
CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF there: the governor and s2idle stay on the first
entry, the WFI the CPUs idle in today, until the second one is enabled
through sysfs.

The driver is the Asahi Linux contributors' cpuidle-apple; the T8140
handling reused here is from Ryan Murray and Bartosz Nitka.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 474e2bc3edb122d94e140af5a07ba85962cc1c4a)
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
index 64b45dcbaf..ba52a80fbc 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@ static struct cpuidle_driver apple_idle_driver = {
 
 static int apple_cpuidle_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	bool t604x = of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node, "apple,t6041-cpuidle");
+
 	/*
 	 * CPU PD writes CYC_OVRD, which is an undefined instruction on
 	 * T8140. Its WFI already lets the hardware power-gate idle
@@ -131,13 +133,23 @@ static int apple_cpuidle_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * the generic s2idle selector skips fallback index 0, otherwise
 	 * tick_freeze() and timekeeping suspension are never reached.
 	 */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8140"))
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8140") || t604x)
 		apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_PWRDOWN] = apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_WFI];
 
+	/*
+	 * T6040 (M4 Pro) is the same: iBoot locks CYC_OVRD, and a plain
+	 * WFI already powers the core down, losing x0-x15 and FP/SIMD
+	 * (the arm64 idle code saves those). Keep the second state off
+	 * until it is enabled through sysfs.
+	 */
+	if (t604x)
+		apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_PWRDOWN].flags |= CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF;
+
 	return cpuidle_register(&apple_idle_driver, NULL);
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id apple_cpuidle_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t6041-cpuidle" },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8140-cpuidle" },
 	{ }
 };
